## Agents-Ready Local Tooling

- Use `./local up` to start local services.
- Use `./local npm install` before starting Vite in a fresh checkout.
- Use `./local test` after application changes.
- Use `./local worktree list` and `./local worktree status` to inspect managed checkout state.
- Use `./local worktree create <path> --branch <branch> [--id <id>]` for linked local worktrees after Agents-Ready generated files are committed.
- Worktrees share the project Postgres and Valkey containers, with per-worktree database names plus Redis prefixes. Horizon prefixes apply only when Horizon is enabled.
- Do not require Laravel Sail; `./local sail ...` forwards to this project's wrapper.
